  "versionNotes": [
    {
      "edition": "ASP.NET Core 11 / .NET 11 GA checked 2026-11-20",
      "items": [
        "ASP.NET Core 11 generates OpenAPI 3.2 by default; .NET 10 generated 3.1 by default. Explicitly select 3.1 when downstream tooling cannot consume 3.2.",
        "ASP.NET Core 11 upgrades Microsoft.OpenApi to 3.x, which changes transformer-facing model APIs; custom transformers written against 2.x may need source changes.",
        "ASP.NET Core 11 OpenAPI adds binary file response descriptions, HTTP QUERY operation descriptions for OpenAPI 3.2, and SSE itemSchema descriptions. Do not claim these are available in an OpenAPI 3.1 document.",
        "HTTP QUERY is standardized in RFC 10008 (June 2026), not merely a proposed method. It is safe and idempotent, carries query content with a media type, and resources can advertise supported formats with Accept-Query. OpenAPI 3.2 has a native query operation field; OpenAPI 3.0/3.1 use the x-oai-additionalOperations extension representation in the ASP.NET Core generator.",
        "Deprecation and Sunset are distinct standardized response headers: RFC 9745 Deprecation signals lifecycle status, while RFC 8594 Sunset indicates an expected date when the resource may become unresponsive.",
        "API versioning remains a separate Asp.Versioning package family rather than a built-in ASP.NET Core feature. The old Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Versioning package family is deprecated; keep exact third-party package APIs labeled as such.",
        "Asp.Versioning releases are independent of the .NET runtime. NuGet versions checked 2026-11-20: Abstractions 10.2.1, MVC 10.2.1, MVC.ApiExplorer 10.2.1, HTTP 10.2.3, and OpenApi 10.2.3. Check each package compatibility rather than assuming family-wide version alignment.",
        "ASP.NET Core 11 UseExceptionHandler preserves BadHttpRequestException.StatusCode by default in Problem Details responses. Applications that depended on conversion to 500 should review their custom exception handling.",
        "Asp.Versioning 10.2 adds ApiVersionRange and compiler analyzers; analyzers are enabled by default and can surface build diagnostics when upgrading. NuGet package versions can differ across family packages.",
        "Asp.Versioning 10.2 also adds VisibleInApiVersionAttribute for versioned model members and IAnnotation<TKey,TValue> for out-of-band member metadata; member filtering changes serialization/schema shape, not authorization."
      ],
